-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party software in the Docker images
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The Docker images of this artifact also contain the following third-party
software, each under its own license; the full texts of the licenses are in
the images at the given paths (~ is /home/tacas27).

* OpenSMT -- MIT license
  Copyright (c) 2008 - 2012 Roberto Bruttomesso, 2012 - 2022 Antti Hyvarinen,
  2018 - 2024 Martin Blicha, 2024 - 2025 Tomas Kolarik
  ~/spexplain/build/_deps/opensmt-src/LICENSE

* Marabou (the verifier of SpExplAIn, and the verifier of VeriX-plus) --
  modified BSD license (BSD-3-Clause), copyright (C) by its authors and
  contributors; it includes third-party libraries (e.g., Boost, OpenBLAS,
  protobuf, ONNX, pybind11) under their own licenses, listed in the same file
  ~/spexplain/build-marabou/_deps/marabou-src/COPYING
  ~/VeriX-plus/Marabou/COPYING

* VeriX-plus (https://github.com/minwu-cs/VeriX-plus), with a patch of the
  original experiments of the paper -- BSD-3-Clause
  Copyright (c) 2022, NeuralNetworkVerification
  ~/VeriX-plus/LICENSE

* The Python packages of VeriX-plus (e.g., NumPy, SciPy, pandas, PyTorch, ONNX,
  ONNX Runtime, Matplotlib, scikit-image, and their dependencies) -- mostly BSD,
  MIT and Apache-2.0 licenses; bound-propagation is under the GNU GPL v3
  ~/VeriX-plus/venv/lib/python3.8/site-packages/*.dist-info/

* uv (the installer of the Python of VeriX-plus) -- MIT or Apache-2.0 license
  Copyright (c) Astral Software Inc.

* The packages of the Debian GNU/Linux base system and the tools installed from
  it (e.g., Python and its packages, TeX Live, GNU parallel, Z3, cvc5, MuPDF) --
  various free software licenses, including the GNU GPL, LGPL and AGPL;
  the sources are available from the Debian archive (https://www.debian.org)
  /usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party datasets
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The datasets of the experiments (in ~/spexplain/data/datasets/ of the images)
are samples of the following datasets, scaled to [0, 1]; they remain under the
terms of the original datasets.

* Heart attack risk: Janosi, A., Steinbrunn, W., Pfisterer, M., Detrano, R.:
  Heart Disease. UCI Machine Learning Repository (1989),
  https://doi.org/10.24432/C52P4X -- CC BY 4.0

* Obesity: Palechor, F.M., Manotas, A.D.l.H.: Estimation of Obesity Levels Based
  On Eating Habits and Physical Condition. UCI Machine Learning Repository
  (2019), https://doi.org/10.24432/C5H31Z -- CC BY 4.0

* Loan: Lo, T.w.: Loan approval classification dataset (2024),
  https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/taweilo/loan-approval-classification-data
  -- Apache License 2.0

* MNIST: LeCun, Y., Cortes, C., Burges, C.J.C.: The MNIST database of
  handwritten digits -- CC BY-SA 3.0

* CIFAR-10: Krizhevsky, A.: Learning multiple layers of features from tiny
  images. Tech. rep., University of Toronto (2009),
  https://www.cs.toronto.edu/~kriz/cifar.html -- no explicit license

* GTSRB: Stallkamp, J., Schlipsing, M., Salmen, J., Igel, C.: The German Traffic
  Sign Recognition Benchmark: A multi-class classification competition. IJCNN
  (2011), https://benchmark.ini.rub.de -- under the terms of its website
